# Tables: the Row with its Style, its Typography, its Id and a Box painted as a band under its cells.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Tables · Row look
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Styles:
		For style: total
			Typography:
				Bold: true
				Color: accent
		For style: link
			Typography:
				Color: accent
	Section:
		Text: Tables
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Row look
		Paragraph: A `Row` passes its `Typography` to its cells, and its `Style` and `Id` rules apply to each of them. Its `Box` takes only `Background`, `Border`, `Border color`, `Border style` and `Corner radius`, painted as one band from the first column to the last, also over the `Gap`.
			Style: intro
		Table:
			Column sizes: * 80
			Column align: left right
			Gap: 0 8
			Header rows:
				Row:
					Box:
						Border: 0 0 1 0
						Border color: accent
					Typography:
						Bold: true
					Cell: Item
					Cell: Amount
			Body rows:
